WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.735
New details of the Ron DeSantis

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.703
for president launch the timing.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:04.471
CNN is told

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.405
the official paperwork

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:06.539
will be filed next week.

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:07.574
That is a necessary

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:08.942
legal step for fundraising

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.744
and other campaign nuts and bolts.

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:11.311
The battle

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.346
plan, though, is much more interesting.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.348
A plan, CNN reports,

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.816
to run to the right of Trump

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.151
on abortion, on guns

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.787
and more time frames it this way.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.289
What Ron DeSantis means for America.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.825
Yes, this is very, very much about him

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.360
and whether the Florida governor

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.962
can rebound from recent struggles

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.397
and seriously challenge Donald

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:32.699
Trump's grip on today's GOP.

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.501
But it is also about much more,

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.402
including the fault

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.903
lines of America's culture wars

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:37.837
and the fault lines

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.539
of our political polarization.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.974
And if what it takes

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.876
to win the Republican nomination

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.077
will make the winner, then

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.212
a tough sell, maybe an impossible sell

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:46.780
in the places

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.515
that settle presidential elections.

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:49.382
With me in studio

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.283
to share their reporting

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.251
and their insights,

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.952
Jackie Kucinich of The Boston Globe,

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.188
Simon Kim, The Associated Press,

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:55.722
to Mitchell

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.357
of The Atlanta Journal-Constitution,

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:57.724
and Amy

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.793
Walter of the Cook Political Report,

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.428
Finally here, we knew it was coming.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.762
He was waiting for the legislature

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:03.129
to end.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.230
Whether that was the right decision

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:04.964
or the wrong decision,

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.132
the voters will tell us

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:07.500
seven, eight months from now.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.234
But here's the Ron

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:08.935
DeSantis push

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.503
at the end of that legislative session.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:11.471
And our reporters

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.606
are told the foundation of his campaign,

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.275
a six week ban on abortion,

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.477
ending concealed weapon permits,

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:18.578
banning gender affirming

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.479
care for transgender

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.414
youth, restricting drag shows, expanding

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.682
the don't say gay law in Florida,

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.584
blocking the AP Advanced Placement

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:25.518
African-American Studies

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.620
Program prohibiting vaccine mandates.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:30.123
This is Ron DeSantis, plan to what?

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.658
Tell Republican voters

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:33.726
I'm Trumpy with results.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.895
I get things done without the drama.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:36.429
What is right?

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:36.729
Well,

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:37.864
he laid that out

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:40.166
in Iowa last weekend, where

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.701
basically what he said is

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.671
you can be successful and a conservative.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.672
You don't just have to go.

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:46.773
I think he said something about

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.808
just posturing on social media.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:51.377
Or sort of turning yourself into a brand.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.413
You can actually bring results.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:54.180
Now, you're right.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.215
Do these results

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:58.718
also help him in a primary but hurt him

00:01:58.718 --> 00:01:59.986
with swing voters?

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:00.820
We have yet to see.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:03.123
I mean, what we know with swing voters is

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:03.990
some of those issues

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.058
are going to be unpopular,

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:07.160
especially on the abortion issue.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.962
But so much of why

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:09.863
the swing voters

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.831
moved off of Donald Trump

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.466
or stuck with Democrats in

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.567
these past few years

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.270
are about things like January 6th

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:19.272
were a feeling that

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:23.143
Donald Trump himself, just that the style

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:26.579
and the way he conducted himself

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.615
was chaotic.

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.316
Was unpredictable.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.050
Versus

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:31.951
if we're going to have a fight

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.753
over policy

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:34.387
that feels like

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:35.622
a very different conversation

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.523
than we're having a fight

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:38.691
over the personal

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:39.325
like we did

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.794
for so much of 20, 16, 20, 20 and

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.596
everything in between.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.031
And so that's his challenge,

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.533
first with Republican voters

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.401
who have a great affinity for Trump

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.769
But so I want to listen to a little bit

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:50.603
of how Ron DeSantis face,

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.038
because what you just said is important.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:52.839
Ron DeSantis says

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:53.806
maybe you disagree with me

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:54.674
on some of these issues,

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.476
but look at Florida. It works.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:58.044
And he uses the term normal

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.582
What we've said in Florida is

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:05.185
we are going to remain a refuge of sanity

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.453
and a citadel of normalcy.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:10.390
And kids should have an upbringing that

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.559
that reflects that

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:14.761
Some of this you look at going

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.094
young guns

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.663
victory in the Virginia governor's race.

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:17.297
There are certainly

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:18.364
a lot of parental concerns

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:19.999
about what's happening in schools.

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:20.934
I guess the question is,

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:21.601
when will we know?

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.602
How do we know

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:23.870
if some of these Republicans

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:24.871
it's not just Florida.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.839
You see the trans policies in Texas

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.007
and other states as well.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.776
Are they going so far to the right

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:30.543
that that,

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:30.810
you know,

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.811
that suburban voters

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:32.912
think this is a solution

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.380
in search of a problem?

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:34.681
Right.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:34.881
Right.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.683
Well, I think on that specific issue,

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:38.685
it hasn't been really tested

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:39.519
